    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green (1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. The identifiers now derive through a version\u20112 algorithm mixing in a fixed `V2` tag, the response groups them and reports `apiVersion`, and the audit event moves to schema v2 \u2014 while `locality`/`timezone`/the segment's region stay the plain region code.\n\n**Identity derivation (`Owner.java`)**\n- Added `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"`, the single definition of the tag.\n- `getIdentityRegionCode()` now returns `\"V2\" + regionCode` (e.g. `V2NSW`, `V2UNKNOWN`) \u2014 the region baked *inside* identifiers. This flows into `memberId`, whose `REGION` segment is now `V2\u2026`.\n- `identityKey(...)` now mixes the `V2` tag into the hashed input, so every identity key changes (both sides of duplicate detection add the same tag, so semantics are preserved).\n\n**householdId (`OwnerRestControllerV1.householdKey`)**\n- The household key now appends `|V2`, so `householdId` changes while the household still keys purely on `(lastName, postcode)`.\n\n**Response shape (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`)**\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema groups `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`; these were removed from the top level.\n- `Owner` gains a nested `identity` object and a top\u2011level integer `apiVersion` (2). The mapper populates both.\n- `locality` still derives from the plain region (`NSW`), independent of the V2 identifier encoding.\n\n**Audit event (`OwnerRestControllerV1.emitOwnerCreatedEvent`)**\n- Schema v2: added `schemaVersion: 2` and `ownerSegment` (recomputed via the mapper from the plain region + membership level). Observed output:\n  `{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`\n\nEvery produced identifier is distinct from any version\u20111 value: V2\u2011prefixed member ids and region codes can't equal the old `NSW\u2026`/`UNKNOWN` forms, and the hash\u2011based `householdId`/`identityKey` take a different preimage. Request fields are unchanged. `./mvnw -o test` passes.",
