    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. `POST /api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (V1; the V2 controller only exposes a paged list). Here is the full ordered pipeline.\n\n## `POST /api/owners` \u2014 ordered pipeline\n\nLegend: **[V]** = validation (throws \u2192 4xx via the exception advice), **[S]** = side-effect / mutation.\n\n### A. Entry \u2014 `addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1:146`)\n1. **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`; caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **[S] Read `Idempotency-Key` header** (`idempotencyKey()`) \u2014 trimmed; blank/absent \u2192 treated as none.\n3. **[V/short-circuit] Idempotent replay** (`replayIdempotentCreate`) \u2014 if that key already produced an owner that still exists, return **200 OK** with the original owner and stop (no new owner, none of the steps below run).\n\n### B. Effective registration date \u2014 `effectiveRegistrationDate` (`:623`)\n4. **[V] Future-date check** \u2014 a supplied `registrationDate` after today \u2192 `InvalidFieldsException` (400, field `registrationDate`).\n5. **[S] Default + business-day roll** \u2014 use supplied date else `now()`, then `toBusinessDay` rolls Saturdays/Sundays/listed 2026 public holidays forward to the next business day. This adjusted date is what everything downstream uses.\n\n### C. Intake rules \u2014 `prepareNewOwner` (`:556`), in this exact order\n6. **[S] Address normalization** (`applyAddress`) \u2014 prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (normalized, and flat `address` recomposed from them); otherwise normalizes the flat `address`. Normalization trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. Runs *before* the required-field check so a blank-after-normalization address is caught.\n7. **[V] Required fields** (`validateRequiredFields`) \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank \u2192 `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (400, `errors` array of all offenders).\n8. **[V/S] Telephone normalization** (`normalizeTelephone`) \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets, forms E.164 (assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0` when no `+`), requires `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, then `validateNationalNumberLength` enforces per-country length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidFieldsException` (400, `telephone`). Stored normalized in place.\n9. **[V/S] Email normalization** (`normalizeEmail`) \u2014 optional (`null` allowed); if present must match the email pattern and its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); stored lower-cased. Invalid/disposable \u2192 `InvalidFieldsException` (400, `email`).\n10. **[V] Postcode** (`validatePostcode`) \u2014 optional; if present must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in that range \u2192 else `InvalidFieldsException` (400, `postcode`).\n11. **[V] Hard duplicate identity** (`rejectDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true`, computes the identity key (SHA-256 over normalized telephone + canonical email + Soundex of last name); if any non-deleted owner already has it \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n12. **[V] City capacity** (`rejectCityAtCapacity`) \u2014 if the city (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (409).\n13. **[V] Daily limit** (`rejectDailyLimitExceeded`) \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already carry the adjusted registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n### D. Build & derive the entity \u2014 `createOwner` (`:216`)\n14. **[S] Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n15. **[S] Set `registrationDate`** to the adjusted business-day date.\n16. **[S] Derive `memberId`** (`memberIdFor`) \u2014 `<REGION><FY><HASH8><LuhnCheck>`, then de-duplicated against existing member ids (`-2`, `-3`, \u2026).\n17. **[S] Set `namesakeCount`** \u2014 count of pre-existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n18. **[S] Assign `householdId`** (`assignHousehold`) \u2014 SHA-256-derived from `(lastName, postcode, V2 tag)`; `null` when no postcode.\n19. **[S] Set soft-duplicate flags** (`applyPossibleDuplicate`) \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`; skipped when `sharesHousehold`; matches on Soundex(lastName)+postcode with a differing identity key.\n20. **[S] Set `membershipLevelCap`** (`householdMembershipLevelCap`) \u2014 one above the max membership level of existing non-deleted household members, else `null`.\n\n### E. Persist & post-persist side-effects\n21. **[S] `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 persists; owner gets its generated id.\n22. **[S] Stamp `householdMemberCount`** (`applyHouseholdMemberCount`) \u2014 now includes the just-saved owner.\n23. **[S] Human-readable audit line** (`auditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 `AUDIT` logger: id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n24. **[S] Structured `OWNER_CREATED` event** (`emitOwnerCreatedEvent`) \u2014 increments the shared `OWNER_CREATED_SEQ` and emits schema-v2 JSON (seq, schemaVersion, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, ownerSegment, event) to `AUDIT`.\n25. **[S] Welcome notification** (`enqueueWelcomeNotification`) \u2014 `NOTIFY` logger: id, memberId.\n\n### F. Response assembly \u2014 back in `addOwner` \u2192 `createdOwnerResponse` (`:365`)\n26. **[S] Record idempotency mapping** \u2014 if a key was supplied, store `key \u2192 owner.id` in the shared `IDEMPOTENT_CREATES` map.\n27. **[S] Build 201 Created** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and derives read-time fields `bulkSignupWarning` (> 80 owners that day), `capacityWarning` (city holds 40\u201349), and `riskFlag` (soft-duplicate OR disposable-adjacent email OR city capacity warning); attaches a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the daily-limit, city-capacity, namesake, duplicate, and member-id-dedup checks each call `clinicService.findAllOwners()` and scan in memory (not DB queries), and several validation limits (100/day, 50/city) and the idempotency/sequence state are held in **static** in-memory fields shared across all requests \u2014 so despite the \"standard Spring conventions\" framing in CLAUDE.md, this create path is heavily customized rather than a plain CRUD insert."
